      "problem": "$2x\\sqrt{45}+x\\sqrt{x}-2x\\sqrt{5}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We simplify each of the radical terms using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x\\sqrt{45}+x\\sqrt{x}-2x\\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ 2x\\sqrt{9\\cdot 5}+x\\sqrt{x}-2x\\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ 2x\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{5}+x\\sqrt{x}-2x\\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ 2x\\cdot 3\\sqrt{5}+x\\sqrt{x}-2x\\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ 6x\\sqrt{5}+x\\sqrt{x}-2x\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we combine the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x\\sqrt{5}+x\\sqrt{x}-2x\\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ (6x-2x)\\sqrt{5}+x\\sqrt{x} & = \\\\ 4x\\sqrt{5}+x\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
